    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Flags spikes and dips per series against a robust rolling median and MAD baseline with weekday effects, centred or trailing.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Time Series",
    "tags": [
        "anomaly detection",
        "outliers",
        "time series",
        "monitoring",
        "robust z-score",
        "MAD",
        "alerts",
        "data quality",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Flags **unusual days, weeks or months** in one or many time series (per store, product, region, sensor, account) against a robust baseline.\n\n- Optionally **aggregates** rows to day, week or month (sum, mean or count of rows); empty periods count as zero for sums and counts, so a missing day of data shows up\n- For daily data, a **weekday effect** is allowed for, so a quiet Sunday or a busy Saturday is not an anomaly (automatic, always, or off)\n- **Baseline**: rolling median of the series, **centred** for reviewing history or **trailing** (past only) to mimic live monitoring\n- **Robust z-score**: (value - expected) / (1.4826 x rolling MAD). The median and MAD are not pulled about by the anomalies themselves\n- |z| above the threshold (3.5 by default) is a **spike** or a **dip**; lower and upper bounds are included for charting a band\n\nOutputs: every period with expected value, bounds, z and flag; the anomalies ranked by severity; and a summary per series with the latest status.",
